          <p>
            The example is exaggerated to make the point, but the pattern is real. Large tubs of whey blends and concentrates generally deliver the lowest cost per 25 g at typical retail prices. Isolates usually sit a step above because of the extra filtering, and organic, grass-fed, or heavily certified products sit higher again. Plant blends vary widely: a plain pea isolate can be very competitive, while premium organic blends with added greens or probiotics are often among the most expensive protein per gram on the shelf.
