          <p>
            Two refinements make the formula more useful. First, run it on the price you would actually pay, including subscription discounts, warehouse-club pricing or a sale, because the same product can move a whole cost tier depending on where you buy it. Second, decide what a higher cost per 25 g is buying you. Paying more for an isolate because lactose upsets you, or for an NSF Certified for Sport product because you are drug tested, is a sound trade. Paying more for a buzzword on the label is not. If you are not sure how many servings a day you need, the <a href="/protein-calculator/">protein calculator</a> will give you a daily target so you can work out monthly cost as well.
